! -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Divertor target profiles for the sheath / HFSHD analysis (model600).
!
! Run:   jorek2_postproc < postproc_targets.in
! Out:   boundary_quantities_s<min>..<max>.dat
!
! Edit the namelist name and the step range below, then feed the .dat to
! util/analyse_targets.py.
!
! EXPRESSION NOTES - both of these are easy to get wrong:
!
!  * T_e / T_i, NOT Te.  The expression called "Te" is T0*fact_T/2 where
!    T0 = Ti + Te, i.e. it returns the MEAN temperature. Its description
!    ("assuming Ti=Te") is only true without WITH_TiTe. T_e and T_i are the
!    real ones (mod_expression.f90:1999-2003).
!
!  * Phi has the WRONG SIGN for model600. The expression is u0*F0/fact_time
!    (mod_expression.f90:1757, flagged "### sign?" in the source), but
!    model600 implements v_pol = +R grad(u) x e_phi, so Phi = -F0*u. The
!    analysis script negates it; if you plot the raw column yourself,
!    remember to flip it or the ExB direction comes out backwards.
!
!  * V_ExB_R/V_ExB_Z ARE consistent with model600 (-R*u_Z, +R*u_R). Safe.
!
!  * `set units 0` is written explicitly above. The default IS 0, but a
!    session that has set it to 1 gives n_e ~ 1e-2 and T_e ~ 1e-3; the analysis
!    script detects that and refuses rather than reporting nonsense.
!
!  * psi_N is exported for reference only. It does NOT separate SOL from PFR -
!    it exceeds 1 on BOTH sides of a separatrix leg. The script uses signed arc
!    length from the strike point instead.
! -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

namelist input

set units 0        ! 0 = SI (Phi in V, T in eV, n in m^-3). REQUIRED - see note below.
set nsub_bnd 4

for step 3800 to 3900 do
  expressions R Z Psi_N Bnorm bnd_normal_R bnd_normal_Z Phi T_e T_i ne V_ExB_R V_ExB_Z
  boundary_quantities
done
